 ## Overview
-Rate-Distortion Joint Finetuning is a training methodology that treats neural network compression and 3D scene representation as a single, unified optimization problem, simultaneously optimizing the model for bitrate efficiency and rendering distortion [S1]. Unlike prior methods that treat compression (quantization) and scene representation as independent stages, this approach integrates a differentiable entropy model directly into the loss function, allowing the network to adapt its feature distributions to minimize the Lagrangian cost of transmission and reconstruction [S1]. It builds on [JointRF Training Procedure](11657-jointrf-training-procedure.md) by introducing specific mechanisms for handling quantization gradients and hierarchical importance weighting.
