 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Gradient Vanishing:** Standard quantization has zero gradients almost everywhere. The uniform noise substitution is critical to enable backpropagation [S1].
-*   **Large Quantization Steps:** Large $Q_{step}$ values can lead to unacceptable performance loss despite the noise injection. This necessitates the Two-step Finetuning Procedure for critical voxels [S1].
-*   **Reference Selection:** The choice of reference graph $G$ affects the residual distribution. Using the preceding voxel is a simple baseline; more refined spatial predictive coding may use interpolation, but complete voxels are preferred for training stability [S1].
